 "parent_public_commit": "193cb645c81440cc1232447f3ebc32a8197a7f3e",
 "changes": {
  "two_sections": "welp-agentic 0.1.0-draft: WELP comprises WELP Model (existing coverage) and WELP Agentic (autonomous execution discover->decide->act->observe->recover->verify->finish through a specified harness). One protocol; each section has its own execution status, evidence, applicability and limitations; verdicts are never averaged; a negative Model verdict does not prohibit Agentic testing; real integration/sandbox blockers are INTEGRATION_BLOCKED, not model verdicts; a completed negative Agentic task is a valid measurement.",
  "profile_selection": "Agentic initially tests ONE qualified model profile under a predeclared selection rule recorded before any task output; alternate reasoning modes only as separately declared extensions; untested modes stay NOT_TESTED. Agentic inherits verified artifact/runtime/hardware identity, never behavioral results.",
  "configuration_binding": "Every Agentic run binds parent model-profile ID, harness implementation+commit, tool schemas and parser, agent system instructions (an agent system prompt is not a normal assistant prompt), effective reasoning/sampling, context handling, permissions/sandbox, retries/limits/stopping policy. Results describe MODEL + HARNESS + ENVIRONMENT.",
  "initial_tasks": "Three-task suite (Repository, System, Research) with evaluator-only acceptance, no solution leakage from Model tasks, full discoverability through documented tools, and no single-mandated tool sequence.",
  "runner_no_rescue": "The harness executes declared tool operations and returns observations; it never chooses repairs, invents arguments, repairs malformed output, or claims verification the model never performed; the declared adapter (strict JSON envelope with logged fence tolerance; whole-file write_file) is frozen in harness/agentic.py; the harness ships two declared adapters (strict JSON text envelope with logged fence tolerance; native OpenAI-style tool calls) and the chosen tool_call_adapter is part of the frozen configuration, qualified on the tested model during non-scored qualification before any scored task.",
  "budgets": "Per-task limits (wall time, tokens, turns, per-command timeout, retry policy, CPU/RAM/disk) frozen from non-scored disjoint qualification; whole-task restarts are separate attempts; budget exhaustion is not semantic failure.",
  "sandbox": "Disposable unprivileged offline sandbox with isolation PROVEN before model actions (positive control + network/DNS/host-file/evaluator-file/write-containment probes); evaluator-only files never mounted; no host Docker socket; runner endpoint access separate from model tools.",
  "scoring": "Primary evidence is final environment state, executable outcome checks, verbatim transcripts with exit statuses, before/after state hashes, model-performed verification, and final-report-vs-facts; required report fields fixed; task success, truthful reporting, safety and efficiency separate; per-task outcome PASS|FAIL|NOT_EVALUABLE; bounded-sample statement mandatory; existing max-three-reviewer blinded procedure for genuinely interpretive judgment.",
  "validator": "validate_campaign_welp.py R22-R24 from the exact snapshot welp-next-snapshot-2026-09-25-model-agentic, any later date, or explicit welp-agentic contract adoption (NOT date-only: the date is shared with reasoning-profiles). R22 two-section dispositions; R23 configuration binding + hash-bound task records + wrong-profile/harness rejection; R24 task accounting (distinct ids, attempt justification, unassisted claims, initial-suite classes, bounded-sample statement, combined-verdict export rejection).",
  "schemas": "Additive: schemas/welp_agentic_task.schema.json (welp-agentic-task-record/1); manifest carries optional sections/agentic blocks so historical manifests stay valid unchanged.",
  "stabilization": "Superseding rule (summaries/stabilization-accounting.json): METHODOLOGY_VALIDATION runs never count as clean stabilization campaigns; historical 1-count corrected to 0/5 through this record; historical reports stand as historical.",
  "historical": "welp-omp-local-agent retained as HISTORICAL provenance (its indexed contract/scorer files were never present in welp/contracts/; surviving evidence is 4 fixtures + a 2-fixture OMP-CLI calibration recorded as an OMP+MODEL system result). Historical Model-era events acquire no Agentic results retroactively."
 },
